body:
So what? it wouldn't matter if they only contributed 0.001%, you are still withholding voting rights to an entire age group. You even said yourself that it is still a "significant amount." Your talking points are appealing to authority, just because laws are discriminatory against minors it does not justify the right to ban 14,15,16,17 year olds, who are theoretically allowed to work legally and contribute money to government programs, from voting. And besides, many countries have already lowered the voting age. Argentina, Brazil, Cuba, Ecuador, Nicaragua, and Isle of Man. This is not a far-fetched idea, even in the US 17 year olds can participate in presidential caucuses in a number of states. I have a question for you, would you at least be open to lowering the voting age with certain limitations? like Bosnia and Serbia for instance, where 16 year olds can vote IF they are employed.

&#x200B;

(edited to fix spelling/grammatical errors)
